 "standard": "ISO 606 (short-pitch transmission precision roller chain, A and B series) and ANSI/ASME B29.1 (precision power transmission roller chain), as published in manufacturers' catalogues and reference pages; edition not stated by the catalogues",
 "source": "Dimensions read from the public catalogues listed in `sources` on 2026-11-06 and cross-checked: a value is kept only where at least two catalogues print it. NOT copied from the standard itself; CadCraft does not hold ISO 606 or ASME B29.1. inches converted with 25.4 exactly.",
 "note": "pitch p, roller diameter d1 (maximum; for chains 25, 35, 04C, 06C the bushing diameter, they have no rollers), inner width b1 (ISO: width between inner plates, minimum; ANSI: nominal roller width), plate = inner (roller-link) plate height h2 (maximum, null when the catalogues disagree). Tolerance for \"the same value\": 0.06 mm (0.10 mm for plate). `checks` names the catalogues that agree on each number and, in `differ`, those that print something else. ANSI and ISO A-series twins (`twin`) are the same chain in two systems; their inner widths are different quantities (nominal vs minimum) and differ by up to 0.3 mm. Tip diameter, seat angle and tooth width are NOT in any source: they stay generator parameters in lib/chain/chain.mjs.",
